@{
    ViewBag.Title = "How Exchanges Work";
}
<main class="container tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:px-4 my-5 tw:my-8 sb-guide-page">
    <header class="sb-page-heading">
        <span class="sb-eyebrow">The exchange, explained</span>
        <h1>Teach one thing.<br />Learn another.</h1>
        <p>SkillBridge supports both mutual skill swaps and one-way mentorships—whether you come ready to teach, to learn, or both.</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="sb-guide-steps">
        <li><span class="sb-guide-number">01</span><div><h2>Set up your profile.</h2><p>Add your name or skip onboarding to browse immediately. Add skills you can teach, skills you want to learn, or both whenever you are ready.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="sb-guide-number">02</span><div><h2>Discover people or communities.</h2><p>Browse reciprocal matches, partial matches, or the full member directory—and reach out anytime with a quick Knock or join topic discussions.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="sb-guide-number">03</span><div><h2>Send a proposal.</h2><p>Ask to learn a skill a member teaches and share your goal, preferred pace, and first meeting idea. The mentor can accept as a two-way swap or a one-way mentorship.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="sb-guide-number">04</span><div><h2>Agree on a plan and learn together.</h2><p>Catalog stages give you a clear roadmap, or you can propose custom milestones together. Both partners confirm each completed stage.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="sb-guide-number">05</span><div><h2>Finish, rate, and grow.</h2><p>When all stages are confirmed, either member completes the exchange and rates the experience. Verified learning progress unlocks smoothly without auto-forcing you to teach.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <aside class="sb-guide-note">
        <h2>Good to know</h2>
        <p>You can read skills and community discussions before signing up. Requests, messages, and exchanges require an account.</p>
        <p>If an exchange cannot continue, either member can end it early and give a reason. It will not count as completed.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="sb-hero-actions">
        <a class="btn tw:inline-flex tw:items-center tw:justify-center tw:gap-2 tw:rounded-xl tw:border-2 tw:border-sb-ink tw:px-4 tw:py-2 tw:font-extrabold tw:shadow-sb-small tw:transition-transform tw:hover:translate-x-[2px] tw:hover:translate-y-[2px] tw:dark:border-sb-night-ink btn-primary tw:bg-sb-blue-strong tw:text-white" href="@Url.Action("Skills", "Explore")">Browse skills</a>
        @if (!User.Identity.IsAuthenticated)
        {
            <a class="btn tw:inline-flex tw:min-h-11 tw:items-center tw:justify-center tw:gap-2 tw:rounded-xl tw:border-2 tw:border-sb-border-control tw:px-4 tw:py-2 tw:font-extrabold tw:shadow-sb-small tw:transition-transform tw:hover:translate-x-[2px] tw:hover:translate-y-[2px] btn-outline-primary tw:bg-sb-card tw:text-sb-blue-strong tw:dark:bg-sb-night-card tw:dark:text-sb-blue-link" href="@Url.Action("Register", "Account")">Create an account</a>
        }
    </div>
</main>
